ed with early morphogenetic events in chick development</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1986</year><volume>320</volume><fpage>447</fpage><lpage>449</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3515198</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hatta</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Okada</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>Takeichi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A monoclonal antibody disrupting calcium-dependent cell&#x02013;cell adhesion of brain tissues: possible role of its target antigen in animal pattern formation</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad  Sci USA</source><year>1985</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>2789</fpage><lpage>2793</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3857614</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hatta</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Takagi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Fujisawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Takeichi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Spatial and temporal expression pattern of N-cadherin cell adhesion molecules correlated with morphogenetic processes of chicken embryos</article-title><source>Dev Biol</source><year>1987</year><volume>120</volume><fpage>215</fpage><lpage>227</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3817290</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hirano</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimoto</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Shimoyama</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirohashi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name>